--- !u!114 &1159471264
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1159471262}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.19607843, g: 0.19607843, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 4680ce3306fdac6459c178d9265ea81f, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 14
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 3
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "I was doing my daily routine but I carelessly made a mistake. Lysinthia
    a girl who is no older than 12 followed me all the way here without me noticing.
    She saw me brutally skewer a squirrel, I paused and panic slowly rose up when
    I realised, she would let everyone know I am the culprit. Before I could make
    a move, she turned and ran towards the village. I chased after her, she may be
    further than me but she is still small and I am used to traverse in this wood
    and managed to quickly close up the gap. I lunged and tackled her to the ground.
    She kicked and screamed while she tried to wriggle out of my grasp. In anger
    and fear I grabbed her throat and closed in. She stopped screaming and now is
    gasping for breath. She was gurgling in her own saliva as I kept tightening my
    grip. I kept going and then *snap* I hear her windpipe snapped and she fell silent.
    I \u2013 I killed her!!! I should be horrified, disgusted at my behaviour. But,
    but why, why do I like it. While I was questioning my behaviour, I dragged her
    body to the depths of the wood. Once I went deep enough, I started to dig a hole
    using my hands. It was hard and rough but with time I managed to make it deep
    enough for her body. I kicked her body in the hole and buried her. After I have
    done the deed, I came to the conclusion that murdering humans feel aeons better
    than I had with animals. It was the exhilarating feeling of committing an act
    that shouldn\u2019t have been committed. After I reached that conclusion, I know
    what must be done\u2026.. "
