--- !u!114 &1648830366
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1648830364}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.19607843, g: 0.19607843, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 4680ce3306fdac6459c178d9265ea81f, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 12
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 1
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 3
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "With each death, some of my memories start coming back. I am Dimitri.
    Every day, I go by my daily routine at the village. Waking up, showering, fishing,
    tending my crops and sell 70% of my harvest while keeping the 30% for the village
    stock which will be our food supply and then, I\u2019ll go back to bed. There
    is nothing else I could do. I am living in a village so hidden that we are not
    marked by any maps that exists in this godforsaken world. Well, we won\u2019t
    have to worry about raids anyway so I am not complaining, but it does get really
    boring very quickly. Well, that changed when I was confronted by two thieves\u2019
    passing by when I was fishing at a nearby river. They brandished their knives
    and demanded me to give me my belongings or else. I didn\u2019t have anything
    on me except for some bait, fishing rod and the yields of my fishing. I didn\u2019t
    want to expose my village\u2019s location either as it will reveal the village
    to them and they may bring in reinforcements who will take control of the village.
    With nothing else to lose, I hoisted my fishing rod which was tightly gripped
    by my sweaty and shaky palms. I first swung the rod towards the nearest thief
    aiming for his head, but I missed and instead hit his arm which made him lose
    grip on the knife he was holding. An unexpected result, but a welcomed one. As
    I tried to steady my pole to aim towards the other thief, I noticed that he was
    crouching and holding his eyes. Blood trailed throughout his arms, and then I
    realised, when the rod hit the first thief the hook and line extended further
    and managed to injure his eyes, disabling him momentarily. I took this golden
    opportunity to hurry towards the knife I knocked out of the thief\u2019s hand.
    I gripped the knife with all my might. I have never used this to harm others
    as we never need to confront enemies. I gulped and threatened the both of them.
    One laughed, mocking my ability to harm them yet alone killing them. they were
    right, I couldn\u2019t kill. I never had too anyways. The uninjured thief lunged
    at me, as he flew towards me, I felt the adrenaline pump throughout my body and
    I jabbed the knife right through his throat.  "
