--- !u!114 &1831125834
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1831125832}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.19607843, g: 0.19607843, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 12800000, guid: 4680ce3306fdac6459c178d9265ea81f, type: 3}
    m_FontSize: 15
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 1
    m_MinSize: 0
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 3
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "The thief gurgled, collapsing and suffocating by his own blood. His friend
    shouted and tried to attack me as well. I moved back in panic and tripped over
    my fishing pole and fell. The thief fell along with as I grabbed his shirt thinking
    it will prevent me from falling but it was to no avail. As we both landed on
    the ground, I expected him to take advantage of this and attack me, but he wasn\u2019t
    moving. It seems when he fell on top of me, he was stabbed by the knife held
    by me. I pushed him away and stood up. I, felt weird. Adrenaline was still pumping
    throughout my body, but I felt something strange. I felt excited. Is it because
    I managed to escape death? Or was it because I killed these thieves? I shouldn\u2019t
    waste my time here, I hastily dug up the ground and dumped both of bodies and
    buried it. Next, I cleaned up the blood from my body and clothes, it took a while
    for the stains to be removed from my shirt but since the blood was still wet,
    I managed to wash it away. I picked up my equipment and fishes I caught as well
    as the knives the thieves held. I might need this in the near future if I need
    to defend myself again. I swallowed my saliva as the adrenaline and excitement
    calmed down and I headed back to the village to continue my daily routine\u2026\u2026
    the routine that is endlessly tiring and unexciting. "
